    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll** (85.84) and **James Wood** (76.28), our undisputed starts against vulnerable arms. **Corbin Carroll** is in a prime position to capitalize on his elite sprint speed and a favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a, with his placement in the three-hole providing the optimal environment for both stolen bases and RBI. Similarly, **James Wood** is slated to leadoff against Spence, whose 6.03 xERA suggests a high-scoring outing; with an xwOBA of .403 and the boost from leadoff volume, he is our highest-upside play for run production. **Gabriel Moreno** (67.76) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (66.04) round out our high-confidence tier, both benefiting from favorable park factors and positive matchups that elevate their daily output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Dalton Rushing** (55.40), who narrowly missed the \"Strong\" threshold due to an unfavorable batting order spot and the potential for a \"hold\" situation against Martinez that could cap his stolen base opportunities. Despite a respectable matchup, the math favored benching players with similar profiles to prioritize total efficiency. We are also closely monitoring the utility spot held by **Kyle Karros** (47.30); while he draws a platoon edge, he is facing an elite arm in Imanaga, which significantly flattens his ceiling. With **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Trevor Story** unavailable due to off-days or injuries, we are leaning heavily on the current active roster to maintain our pace in the 5x5 standings. \n\nManagers should remain alert for any late-breaking lineup changes regarding **Alex Freeland**, who is currently batting in the nine-hole. While his 50.96 score makes him a marginal play, his defensive versatility and the potential for late-inning plate appearances keep him in the fold today. We continue to manage our bench depth\u2014including **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014to ensure our game caps are preserved for the upcoming week while maximizing our exposure to the weakest opposing pitchers on the slate.",
